@c -*-texinfo-*-
@node gpui-themes Manual
@chapter Crate @code{gpui-themes}
@cindex gpui-themes
@cindex themes

@code{gpui-themes} provides theme editing and management for GPUI
applications. It is a serializable theme system with JSON and Rust
export, a colour picker, a component showcase and a built-in theme
editor used to preview themes interactively.

@menu
* gpui-themes User Guide::
* gpui-themes Developer Guide::
@end menu

@node gpui-themes User Guide
@section User Guide

@subheading Switching theme

The desktop player ships several themes (dark, light, high-contrast,
and custom). Pick one from Settings.

@subheading Customising

The bundled theme editor lets you tweak any colour token, see the
result on the component showcase, and export the result as JSON. Drop
the JSON into the user config directory and SotF will pick it up.

@node gpui-themes Developer Guide
@section Developer Guide

@subheading What's in a theme

A theme is a struct of named colour tokens (accent, surface,
text-primary, text-secondary, danger, @dots{}). It is independent of
@ref{gpui-design Manual}: design controls shape and motion, themes
control colour.

@subheading Loading order

@enumerate
@item Built-in default.
@item User-overridden theme JSON from the config directory.
@item Runtime override (e.g.@: from a CLI flag or unit test).
@end enumerate

@subheading Exporters

@itemize @bullet
@item @strong{JSON} -- the canonical user-facing format.
@item @strong{Rust} -- emits a @code{const Theme} declaration suitable
  for embedding into a binary.
@end itemize

@subheading Hooks into other crates

@itemize @bullet
@item @ref{gpui-ui-kit Manual} components read the current theme.
@item @ref{gpui-ui-kit-macros Manual} provides @code{#[derive(ComponentTheme)]}
  to wire a component theme to global tokens with one line.
@item @ref{gpui-d3rs Manual} and @ref{gpui-px Manual} read theme
  colours for chart styling.
@end itemize
